# Lucide React Icons

**Trigger**: Auto-applied to all `.tsx` and `.ts` files importing from `lucide-react`.

## Package

- **Version**: `lucide-react` v1.18.0
- **Source**: [lucide.dev](https://lucide.dev) | [GitHub](https://github.com/lucide-icons/lucide)
- **Already in `package.json`** — do not reinstall.

## Import Patterns

All icons import from the main `lucide-react` package. No SSR/CSR distinction needed.

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT — single import path for all contexts
import { Calendar, CheckCircle, Sparkles } from 'lucide-react';

// ✅ CORRECT — works in both Server and Client Components
import { ArrowRight, X } from 'lucide-react';
```

### No SSR Concerns

Unlike some icon libraries, `lucide-react` has no SSR/hydration issues. Use the same import in:
- Server Components
- Client Components
- shadcn/ui component files

## Icon Naming Convention

### Exported Names

Lucide exports icons in **PascalCase** without suffixes. Use the exact name from the documentation.

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT — PascalCase, no suffix
import { Calendar, CheckCircle, ArrowRight } from 'lucide-react';

// ❌ WRONG — Icon suffix (Phosphor pattern)
import { CalendarIcon, CheckCircleIcon } from 'lucide-react';

// ❌ WRONG — kebab-case
import { arrow-right, check-circle } from 'lucide-react';
```

### Finding Icon Names

- Browse all icons at [lucide.dev/icons](https://lucide.dev/icons)
- Use Ctrl/Cmd+F to search the icon list
- Names match common English terms (e.g., `Calendar`, `CheckCircle`, `ArrowRight`)

## Props and Styling

Icon components accept standard SVG props plus Lucide-specific props:

| Prop | Type | Default | Usage |
|------|------|---------|-------|
| `size` | `number \| string` | `24` | Height & width in pixels. Prefer Tailwind `className="size-4"` |
| `color` | `string` | `"currentColor"` | Stroke color. Use CSS variable tokens via `className` |
| `strokeWidth` | `number` | `2` | Stroke thickness (0.5-3 recommended) |
| `absoluteStrokeWidth` | `boolean` | `false` | Keep stroke width constant when scaling |

### Styling via Tailwind

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — Tailwind classes for size and color
<Calendar className="size-4 text-muted-foreground" />

// ✅ GOOD — strokeWidth for visual weight
<CheckCircle className="size-4 text-success" strokeWidth={2.5} />

// ❌ BAD — inline styles for size/color
<Calendar style={{ width: 16, height: 16, color: '#888' }} />
```

### Color Tokens

Use semantic CSS variables, not hardcoded hex values:

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — semantic token
<CheckCircle className="size-4 text-success" />

// ✅ GOOD — foreground token
<Calendar className="size-4 text-foreground" />

// ❌ BAD — hardcoded color
<CheckCircle className="size-4" color="#22c55e" />
```

## Dynamic Icon Patterns

When mapping icon names to components dynamically, use a lookup object:

```tsx
import { Calendar, FileText, Settings, type LucideIcon } from 'lucide-react';

const iconMap: Record<string, LucideIcon> = {
  calendar: Calendar,
  document: FileText,
  settings: Settings,
};

function DynamicIcon({ name, className }: { name: string; className?: string }) {
  const IconComponent = iconMap[name];
  if (!IconComponent) return null;
  return <IconComponent className={className} />;
}

// Usage
<DynamicIcon name="calendar" className="size-4 text-primary" />
```

## Common Icons Reference

Frequently used icons in this project:

| Use Case | Icon Name | Import |
|----------|-----------|--------|
| Close/dismiss | X | `import { X } from 'lucide-react'` |
| Check/success | Check, CheckCircle | `import { Check, CheckCircle } from 'lucide-react'` |
| Navigation arrows | ArrowLeft, ArrowRight, ChevronDown, ChevronRight | `import { ArrowLeft, ChevronDown } from 'lucide-react'` |
| Actions | Plus, Edit, Trash2, Copy | `import { Plus, Edit, Trash2 } from 'lucide-react'` |
| Status | AlertCircle, Info, AlertTriangle | `import { AlertCircle, Info } from 'lucide-react'` |
| UI elements | Menu, Search, Settings, User | `import { Menu, Search, Settings } from 'lucide-react'` |

## Type Import

When typing icon props or variables:

```tsx
import type { LucideIcon, LucideProps } from 'lucide-react';

// Icon component type
const MyIcon: LucideIcon = Calendar;

// Props type
function IconButton({ iconProps }: { iconProps: LucideProps }) {
  return <Calendar {...iconProps} />;
}
```

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

| Anti-Pattern | Problem | Fix |
|-------------|---------|-----|
| `import { CalendarIcon }` | Wrong naming (Phosphor pattern) | Use `import { Calendar }` |
| Different imports for Server/Client | Unnecessary complexity | Use same import everywhere |
| Hardcoded `color` hex values | Breaks theme/dark mode | Use Tailwind color tokens via `className` |
| Inline `style` for size | Ignores Tailwind scale | Use `className="size-N"` |
| Importing all icons via `import *` | Prevents tree-shaking, bloats bundle | Import individual icons |
| Using kebab-case names | Wrong naming convention | Use PascalCase: `ArrowRight` not `arrow-right` |

## Verification

Before committing changes involving lucide-react:

- [ ] All icons import from `'lucide-react'` (single path)
- [ ] Icon names use PascalCase without suffixes (`Calendar` not `CalendarIcon`)
- [ ] No hardcoded hex/rgb colors on icon `color` prop
- [ ] Icon sizes use Tailwind `className="size-N"` pattern
- [ ] Tree-shaking works (import individual icons, not `import *`)
- [ ] `pnpm run build` passes (no errors)
